{
  "_comment": [
    "Seccomp allowlist for the analyst sandbox (analyst/runner.py) \u2014 Phase 8.",
    "",
    "An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist, and that distinction is the whole file. A",
    "custom seccomp profile REPLACES the runtime's default one rather than",
    "adding to it, so a profile written as 'deny these dangerous calls'",
    "silently permits every call the default profile blocked and nobody",
    "listed. defaultAction is ERRNO here: a syscall is refused unless it is",
    "named below, including syscalls added to the kernel after this was",
    "written.",
    "",
    "ERRNO rather than KILL on purpose. A refused syscall comes back to",
    "Python as OSError, which the runner reports as a failed execution with",
    "a message; SCMP_ACT_KILL_PROCESS produces a container that died with no",
    "output and no explanation, which is the same evidence as a crash.",
    "",
    "Applied to the SANDBOX container only, via SANDBOX_SECCOMP_PROFILE. It",
    "is deliberately NOT applied to the API or worker containers: those run",
    "a web server, a database driver and xgboost, whose syscall surface is",
    "far wider than this, and the runtime's default profile is already an",
    "allowlist and already appropriate for them.",
    "",
    "VERIFY BEFORE TRUSTING: this profile has not been exercised against a",
    "running daemon in this repository \u2014 the machine it was written on had",
    "no Docker daemon available. `python ops/verify_sandbox.py` builds the",
    "image and runs a real analysis through it, and is the check that turns",
    "this from plausible into known. A missing syscall shows up there as an",
    "import failure in numpy or scipy, not as a subtle wrong answer."
  ],
